{"name":"Garden Swing","hex":"#8cbd97","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"},{"term":"swing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To rotate about an off-centre fixed point.","To dance."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act, or an instance, of swinging.","The manner in which something is swung."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swing"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swing (seat)","blocks":[{"text":"A swing is a seat or platform, suspended from chains, ropes, or bars, on which one or more people can swing back and forth for enjoyment or relaxation. Swings are a common piece of equipment at children's playgrounds and may also be found in yards or gardens, on porches, inside homes, or as freestanding public play equipment like the Estonian village swing. Swings have a long history in many different parts of the world and come in various types."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/MoSchaukel.jpg/330px-MoSchaukel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swing_(seat)","wikidata":"Q188688"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki